# G060 — Matrix

*v2. See `matrix.md` for prose: shape-gated operations, matmul inner-dim
compatibility, transpose as shape-swap.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Agent Workload Matrix

[agent-workload-transform
    IN ORDER TO
        compute how much each agent touched each project
        by multiplying the agent-day workload by the day-project priority

    @workload <- [db[load-matrix {table: "allocations"}]]    ;; N × 7
    @priority <- [db[load-matrix {table: "agent-priority"}]]  ;; 7 × K

    @workload
        where columns equal @priority rows (shapes must chain)
        || -> #shape-mismatch "cannot multiply " + @workload:shape + " × " + @priority:shape

    @agent-project <- [matrix[matmul {a: @workload, b: @priority}]]

    @agent-project
        where
            shape is (@workload:rows, @priority:cols)
            and all entries are non-negative
        || -> #sanity-check-failed @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[matrix
    new           {rows}
    zeros         {rows, cols}
    identity      {n}
    shape         {m}
    get           {m, i, j}
    set           {m, i, j, value}
    add           {a, b}              ;; || shape-mismatch
    sub           {a, b}              ;; || shape-mismatch
    scalar-mul    {m, k}
    matmul        {a, b}              ;; || inner-dim-mismatch
    transpose     {m}
    determinant   {m}                  ;; || not-square
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: shape compatibility as `where` precondition

[matrix[matmul {a: @a, b: @b}
    where @a columns equals @b rows
        || resists with "inner-dimension-mismatch: @a:cols vs @b:rows"
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @a <- [matrix[new {rows: [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]}]]     ;; 2×3
    @b <- [matrix[new {rows: [[1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]]}]]   ;; 3×2

    @product <- [matrix[matmul {a: @a, b: @b}]]              ;; 2×2
    -> [matrix[get {m: @product, i: 0, j: 0}]]               ;; -> 4  (1+0+3)
    -> [matrix[get {m: @product, i: 1, j: 1}]]               ;; -> 11 (0+5+6)
    -> [matrix[shape {m: @product}]]                          ;; -> (2, 2)

    @i3 <- [matrix[identity {n: 3}]]
    -> [matrix[determinant {m: @i3}]]                         ;; -> 1
]
